title:: SuperCollider as Plugin in Host
categories:: Guide
summary:: How to use SuperCollider inside VST‑enabled environments such as DAWs and sound file editors.

Description::

DAWs and sound editors include built‑in instruments and effects, which may have limited control over synthesis structure or exhibit aliasing at high frequencies.
SuperCollider provides an alternative workflow via the link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider:: VST3 plug‑in:
design link::Classes/SynthDef::s in SuperCollider, then load and play them within link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider:: in your DAW.

section:: How to Do

numberedlist::

## Install SuperCollider and link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider::

list::
## Verify that SuperCollider is installed and functioning correctly (ensure you can boot the server and run link::Classes/SynthDef:: examples).
## Install PluginCollider from link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider#PluginCollider:: to ensure it appears in your DAW or audio editor's VST plug‑in list.
To install, place the teletype::PluginCollider.vst3:: into either the system default VST3 directory or a user‑defined folder scanned by your host application. The standard installation directories are:


list::
## Linux:

teletype::
~/.vst3/
::


After copying the file, launch your DAW to rescan for VST3 plug‑ins.
If the host application is already running, perform a manual plug‑in rescan or restart the application.


## macOS:

teletype::
/Library/Audio/Plug‑Ins/VST3/
::

(or a custom folder configured in your DAW)

note::
On macOS, the following command is required to authorize link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider:: after installation:

teletype::
sudo xattr -r -d com.apple.quarantine /Library/Audio/Plug‑Ins/VST3/PluginCollider.vst3
::

This command modifies macOS security attributes to bypass Gatekeeper restrictions and requires administrator privileges.
(Execute this command only for software you trust.)
::

## Windows:

teletype::
C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3
::

(or a custom folder configured in your DAW)
::
::

## Design and Test link::Classes/SynthDef::s

list::
## Write your instrument or effect as a link::Classes/SynthDef:: in SuperCollider.
## Test it interactively in teletype::sclang:: to verify sound quality, parameter ranges, and general behavior.
## Decide which arguments you want to control from the DAW (e.g., teletype::amp::, teletype::freq::, teletype::attackTime::) and which ones to keep fixed internally.

## For effects processing in link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider::, link::Classes/SynthDef::s use teletype::SoundIn:: to receive audio directly from the DAW's FX input. No link::Classes/Bus:: setup within the SuperCollider server is required.
::

## Export link::Classes/SynthDef::s

list::
## Use link::Classes/SynthDef#-writeDefFile:: to export the definition into a directory that link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider:: scans for teletype::.scsyndef:: files.

note::
While you can use SuperCollider's default synthdef folder at
code::(Platform.userAppSupportDir +/+ "synthdefs")::, this location contains all teletype::.scsyndef:: files ever created by sclang.
For better organization with link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider::, we recommend using a dedicated folder.
::
::

## Load in DAW or Sound Editor

list::
## Open your DAW or sound editor and insert link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider:: as an instrument on a track (in a DAW) or as an effect from the processing menu (in a sound editor or a DAW).

note::
When using link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider:: for the first time, set the directory containing your teletype::.scsyndef:: files.
::

## Within link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider::'s interface, select the exported link::Classes/SynthDef:: you want to use.

## Save this as part of your DAW project or as a plug‑in preset for use in other projects.
::

## Integrate into Your Workflow

list::
## Use MIDI tracks in your DAW to trigger SuperCollider instruments hosted by link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider::.
## To apply audio effects, insert PluginCollider after the instrument on a MIDI track that supports virtual instruments, or place it on an audio track.
## Automate or control exposed parameters to create dynamic changes over time.
## Apply link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider::‑based effects to audio tracks for additional DSP processing alongside other plugins, and bounce or freeze tracks as needed.
::

::


section:: Examples

subsection:: Using a SynthDef as a VSTi

subsubsection:: Step 1: Design SynthDef and Test in SuperCollider

code::
(
[\sine, \saw, \triangle, \pulse, \additive].do { |name|
	SynthDef(name, { |out = 0, freq = 440, amp = 0.1, pan = 0, phaseR = 1, gate = 1,
		attackTime = 0.07, decayTime = 0.08, sustainLevel = 0.1, releaseTime = 0.3,
		beatByPitchDetune = 0.041666666666667,
		vibDelayFromAttack = 0.2, vibDelayPostTransient = 0,
		vibStartFreq = 3, vibPeakFreq = 7, vibEndFreq = 4, vibAccelTime = 0.4,
		vibAmp = 0.02, vibPitch = 0.0625, randomPercent = 6.25|

		var rand = 2 ** (Rand(randomPercent / -2, randomPercent / 2) / 1200);

		var conflictDetector = (vibDelayFromAttack > 0) * (vibDelayPostTransient > 0);
		var warnTrig = Trig1.kr(conflictDetector, 0.001);

		var transientAtBeginning = attackTime + (decayTime * 1.1);

		var vibStartingAfterTransient = transientAtBeginning + vibDelayPostTransient;
		var delayStartingFromAttack = vibDelayFromAttack;

		var selVibDelayFromAttack = (vibDelayFromAttack > 0) * (vibDelayPostTransient |==| 0);
		var selVibDelayPostTransient = (vibDelayFromAttack |==| 0) * (vibDelayPostTransient > 0);

		var vibDelaySelector = (selVibDelayFromAttack * 1) + (selVibDelayPostTransient * 2);

		var vibDelaySelected = Select.kr(
			vibDelaySelector.poll(0, \vibDelaySelector),
			[
				DC.kr(0).(0, \noVibDelay),
				delayStartingFromAttack.poll(0, \delayStartingFromAttack),
				vibStartingAfterTransient.poll(0, \vibStartingAfterTransient)
			]
		).poll(0, \vibDelaySelected);
		var vibDelayAdapted = vibDelaySelected * rand * amp.max(0).linlin(1, 0, 1, 1.5);

		var vibEnvTimes = [vibDelayAdapted, vibAccelTime, releaseTime / 2.5] * rand;
		var vibSpeedEnv = Env([0, vibStartFreq, vibPeakFreq, vibEndFreq] * rand, vibEnvTimes, \cubed, 2);
		var vibDepthEnv = Env([0, 0, 1, 0],	vibEnvTimes, \cubed, 2);
		var vibDepthEnvGen = EnvGen.kr(vibDepthEnv, gate);

		var lfo = (SinOsc.kr(EnvGen.kr(vibSpeedEnv, gate), -pi/2, 1.557407724655)).atan;

		var vibPitchDepth = vibPitch * vibDepthEnvGen * rand;
		var modulatorPitch = lfo.linlin(-1, 1, 0, 1) * vibPitchDepth;
		var freqModulated = freq * modulatorPitch.midiratio;

		var vibAmpDepth = (vibAmp * vibDepthEnvGen).clip(0, 1);
		var modulatorAmp = lfo.linlin(-1, 1, 0, vibAmpDepth);
		var ampModulated = (1 - modulatorAmp).clip(0, 1);

		var env = Env.adsr(attackTime * rand, decayTime * rand, sustainLevel * rand,
			releaseTime, curve: -4).kr(Done.freeSelf, gate);

		var sig = switch(name,
			\sine, { SinOsc.ar(freqModulated * [1, beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand]) },
			\saw, { Saw.ar(freqModulated * [1, beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand]) },
			\triangle, { LFTri.ar(freqModulated * [1, beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand]) },
			\pulse, { Pulse.ar(freqModulated * [1, beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand], \width.kr(0.5)) },
			\additive, {
				var numHarmonics = 16;
				var synth = { |channelFreqs|
					var frequencies = freqModulated * channelFreqs *.t (1..numHarmonics);
					var amplitudes = \amplitudes.kr(1 ! numHarmonics / numHarmonics);
					var amplitudesModifiedByFreqs = frequencies.size.collect { |i|
						Select.kr(frequencies[i] > (SampleRate.ir / 2), [amplitudes[i], 0])
					};
					DynKlang.ar(
						`[
							frequencies,
							amplitudesModifiedByFreqs,
							\phases.kr(0 ! numHarmonics)
					])
				};
				[synth.(1), synth.(beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand)]
			}
		);

		Poll.kr(
			warnTrig,
			0,
			"WARN: vibDelayFromAttack & vibDelayPostTransient both non-zero.\n" ++
			" No sound is poduced. Set one to"
		);

		sig = sig * ampModulated * env * (1 - conflictDetector);
		sig = LeakDC.ar(sig);

		Out.ar(out, Balance2.ar(sig[0], sig[1] * phaseR, pan, amp));
	}).add
}
)
::

subsubsection:: Step 2: Test in SuperCollider

code::
(
Pbind(
	// \instrument, \sine,               \amp, 0.1,
	// \instrument, \triangle,           \amp, 0.05,
	// \instrument, \saw,                \amp, 0.05,
	// \instrument, \pulse, \width, 0.7, \amp, 0.05,
	\instrument, \additive, \phases, [0!16], \amplitudes, [16.collect ((_ + 1).pow(-0.8) * (_ * 0.15).neg.exp)], \amp, 0.1,
	// \out, 0,
	\freq, Pseq([69, 72, 71, 67, Prand([64, 76])].midicps, inf),
	\pan, 0,		\phaseR, -1,
	// \gate, 1,
	\attackTime, 0.03,     \decayTime, 0.3,     \sustainLevel, 0.25,   \releaseTime, 0.8,
	\beatByPitchDetune, 1/20, \randomPercent, 3,
	\vibDelayFromAttack, 0.2, \vibDelayPostTransient, 0,
	\vibStartFreq, 3,   \vibPeakFreq, 7,   \vibEndFreq, 4,     \vibAccelTime, 0.4,
	\vibAmp, 0.05,   \vibPitch, 0.05
).play;
)
::


subsubsection:: Step 3: Exporting for PluginCollider

After testing, export the link::Classes/SynthDef:: to a directory that link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider:: scans.
Adjust the path to match your own link::https://github.com/asb2m10/plugincollider##PluginCollider:: SynthDef folder.

note::
Note: In the code snippet below, each code::poll(0, …):: call has been commented out.
These calls are intended solely for debugging in SuperCollider.
::

code::
(
[\sine, \saw, \triangle, \pulse, \additive].do { |name|
	SynthDef(name, { |out = 0, freq = 440, amp = 0.1, pan = 0, phaseR = 1, gate = 1,
		attackTime = 0.07, decayTime = 0.08, sustainLevel = 0.1, releaseTime = 0.3,
		beatByPitchDetune = 0.041666666666667,
		vibDelayFromAttack = 0.2, vibDelayPostTransient = 0,
		vibStartFreq = 3, vibPeakFreq = 7, vibEndFreq = 4, vibAccelTime = 0.4,
		vibAmp = 0.02, vibPitch = 0.0625, randomPercent = 6.25|

		var rand = 2 ** (Rand(randomPercent / -2, randomPercent / 2) / 1200);

		var conflictDetector = (vibDelayFromAttack > 0) * (vibDelayPostTransient > 0);
		var warnTrig = Trig1.kr(conflictDetector, 0.001);

		var transientAtBeginning = attackTime + (decayTime * 1.1);

		var vibStartingAfterTransient = transientAtBeginning + vibDelayPostTransient;
		var delayStartingFromAttack = vibDelayFromAttack;

		var selVibDelayFromAttack = (vibDelayFromAttack > 0) * (vibDelayPostTransient |==| 0);
		var selVibDelayPostTransient = (vibDelayFromAttack |==| 0) * (vibDelayPostTransient > 0);

		var vibDelaySelector = (selVibDelayFromAttack * 1) + (selVibDelayPostTransient * 2);

		var vibDelaySelected = Select.kr(
			vibDelaySelector/*.poll(0, \vibDelaySelector)*/,
			[
				DC.kr(0)/*.(0, \noVibDelay)*/,
				delayStartingFromAttack/*.poll(0, \delayStartingFromAttack)*/,
				vibStartingAfterTransient/*.poll(0, \vibStartingAfterTransient)*/
			]
		)/*.poll(0, \vibDelaySelected)*/;
		var vibDelayAdapted = vibDelaySelected * rand * amp.max(0).linlin(1, 0, 1, 1.5);

		var vibEnvTimes = [vibDelayAdapted, vibAccelTime, releaseTime / 2.5] * rand;
		var vibSpeedEnv = Env([0, vibStartFreq, vibPeakFreq, vibEndFreq] * rand, vibEnvTimes, \cubed, 2);
		var vibDepthEnv = Env([0, 0, 1, 0],	vibEnvTimes, \cubed, 2);
		var vibDepthEnvGen = EnvGen.kr(vibDepthEnv, gate);

		var lfo = (SinOsc.kr(EnvGen.kr(vibSpeedEnv, gate), -pi/2, 1.557407724655)).atan;

		var vibPitchDepth = vibPitch * vibDepthEnvGen * rand;
		var modulatorPitch = lfo.linlin(-1, 1, 0, 1) * vibPitchDepth;
		var freqModulated = freq * modulatorPitch.midiratio;

		var vibAmpDepth = (vibAmp * vibDepthEnvGen).clip(0, 1);
		var modulatorAmp = lfo.linlin(-1, 1, 0, vibAmpDepth);
		var ampModulated = (1 - modulatorAmp).clip(0, 1);

		var env = Env.adsr(attackTime * rand, decayTime * rand, sustainLevel * rand,
			releaseTime, curve: -4).kr(Done.freeSelf, gate);

		var sig = switch(name,
			\sine, { SinOsc.ar(freqModulated * [1, beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand]) },
			\saw, { Saw.ar(freqModulated * [1, beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand]) },
			\triangle, { LFTri.ar(freqModulated * [1, beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand]) },
			\pulse, { Pulse.ar(freqModulated * [1, beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand], \width.kr(0.5)) },
			\additive, {
				var numHarmonics = 16;
				var synth = { |channelFreqs|
					var frequencies = freqModulated * channelFreqs *.t (1..numHarmonics);
					var amplitudes = \amplitudes.kr(1 ! numHarmonics / numHarmonics);
					var amplitudesModifiedByFreqs = frequencies.size.collect { |i|
						Select.kr(frequencies[i] > (SampleRate.ir / 2), [amplitudes[i], 0])
					};
					DynKlang.ar(
						`[
							frequencies,
							amplitudesModifiedByFreqs,
							\phases.kr(0 ! numHarmonics)
					])
				};
				[synth.(1), synth.(beatByPitchDetune.midiratio * rand)]
			}
		);

		Poll.kr(
			warnTrig,
			0,
			"WARN: vibDelayFromAttack & vibDelayPostTransient both non-zero.\n" ++
			" No sound is poduced. Set one to"
		);

		sig = sig * ampModulated * env * (1 - conflictDetector);
		sig = LeakDC.ar(sig);

		Out.ar(out, Balance2.ar(sig[0], sig[1] * phaseR, pan, amp));
	}).writeDefFile(Platform.userAppSupportDir +/+ "Help" +/+ "Guides")
}
)
::


subsection:: Using an Effect

You can also define DSP effects as link::Classes/SynthDef::s for use as insert or send effects in your DAW.
This example shows a delay effect with dynamically varying delay time using link::Classes/DelayC:: that processes incoming host audio.

subsubsection:: Step 1: Design SynthDef and Test in SuperCollider

code::
(
SynthDef(\dynamicdelays, { |varyingDelayTime = 10, mix = 0, amp = 1|
	var dry, delayTime, wet, mixed, panned;
	dry = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]).sum / 2;
	delayTime = SinOsc.ar(varyingDelayTime.reciprocal).range(0.5, 10);
	wet = DelayC.ar(dry, 10, delayTime, amp);
	wet = Limiter.ar(wet, 0.9, 0.01);
	mixed = XFade2.ar(dry, wet, mix);
	panned = Pan2.ar(mixed, SinOsc.ar(varyingDelayTime), amp);
	Out.ar(0, panned);
}).add
)
::

subsubsection:: Step 2: Test in SuperCollider

code::
x = Synth(\dynamicdelays) // Warning: The sound could be very loud!

x.free
::

subsubsection:: Step 3: Exporting for PluginCollider

code::
(
SynthDef(\dynamicdelays, { |varyingDelayTime = 10, mix = 0, amp = 1|
	var dry, delayTime, wet, mixed, panned;
	dry = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]).sum / 2;
	delayTime = SinOsc.ar(varyingDelayTime.reciprocal).range(0.5, 10);
	wet = DelayC.ar(dry, 10, delayTime, amp);
	wet = Limiter.ar(wet, 0.9, 0.01);
	mixed = XFade2.ar(dry, wet, mix);
	panned = Pan2.ar(mixed, SinOsc.ar(varyingDelayTime), amp);
	Out.ar(0, panned);
}).writeDefFile(Platform.userAppSupportDir +/+ "Help" +/+ "Guides");
)
::

subsection:: In a DAW (Reaper Example)

Refer to steps 4 and 5 in link::#How to Do:: to experiment with the following link::https://www.reaper.fm/##Reaper:: project, which includes the two examples above:

code::
(Platform.userAppSupportDir +/+ "Help" +/+ "Guides" +/+ "SC_as_Plugin.RPP").openOS
::
